# Dotted tokens in the shipped text that are NOT .claude/ds-config.json keys, so
# scripts/check-config-keys.py does not require them in schemas/seam-registry.json.
# One token per line, then its reason. A real config key never belongs here: register it.
user.login            a GitHub API field (review-thread authors)
github.actor          a GitHub Actions context value
attachment.id         a DevStride API field in a worked example
directedBy.email      a field of the agent session summary payload, not a config key
statusLine.command    a Claude Code settings.json key, not a ds-config key
ci.concurrency        a per-workflow fact setup's CI detection records in its report
ci.productionTreeSkip a per-workflow fact setup's CI detection records in its report
ci.policyCheck        a per-workflow fact setup's CI detection records in its report
